content.text:
The user-visible degradation is in the travel-plan endpoints (`minStation`, `cheapest`, `quickest`), reached through `ts-ui-dashboard`. It traces back to one root cause: a brief pod failure of `ts-travel2-service`.

**Root cause: `ts-travel2-service`, pod_failure.** Travel2 went quiet around 04:32:41 and resumed at 04:33:32 with its restart counter going from 0 to 1. Route-plan's calls to travel2 failed with "connection refused" during that window. The failed attempts were recovered by retries and then surfaced as errors higher up the chain. Travel2's CPU spike (about 2.5 cores in 04:33, then about 0.18) looks like a restart transient. Travel2's own server spans stay normal once it's back, so the fault did not propagate inside travel2 itself.

**Propagation:** travel2 → route-plan (503s on outgoing POSTs, then 500 on `minStopStations`) → travel-plan (500s and roughly 11 s calls on `minStation`) → ui-dashboard (`minStation` average rose from about 844 ms to 1631 ms, max 20 s) → users.

I didn't check every service's resource metrics, and the other background warnings (food-service, order-other-service) appear in both periods, so I didn't count them as faults.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel2-service",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name AS pod, metric, min(value) AS mn, max(value) AS mx FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'ts-travel2%' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "ts-travel2-service pod restart counter is 1 during the incident, versus 0 in the normal period."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT substr(CAST(time AS VARCHAR),1,16) AS mn, sum((service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind='Client' AND attr_http_response_status_code=503)::INT) AS r503, sum((service_name='ts-travel2-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server')::INT) AS travel2_srv, sum((service_name='ts-travel-service' AND attr_span_kind='Server')::INT) AS travel_srv FROM abnormal_traces GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
          "claim": "Route-plan's 503 POSTs occur only at 04:32-04:33, when travel2 emits no server spans; they resume afterwards."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message, attr_k8s_pod_name, count(*) c FROM abnormal_logs WHERE level='SEVERE' AND service_name='ts-route-plan-service' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Route-plan logs 503 'upstream connect error ... Connection refused' from its outgoing calls, 64 times."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT substr(CAST(time AS VARCHAR),1,16) AS mn, round(avg(value),2) AS cpu FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='container.cpu.usage' AND attr_k8s_pod_name LIKE 'ts-travel2%' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
          "claim": "Travel2 CPU spikes to about 2.5 during restart minute 04:33, then settles around 0.18."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-travel2-service",
      "to": "ts-route-plan-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p.attr_http_response_status_code AS st, c.service_name AS callee, count(*) AS n, round(avg(p.duration)/1e6,1) AS ms FROM abnormal_traces p LEFT JOIN abnormal_traces c ON c.parent_span_id=p.span_id AND c.trace_id=p.trace_id AND c.attr_span_kind='Server' WHERE p.service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND p.attr_span_kind='Client' AND p.span_name='POST' GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Route-plan's 64 failed 503 POSTs have no downstream child span, while successful POSTs reach travel and travel2."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-route-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT p.attr_http_response_status_code AS st, count(*) AS n, round(avg(p.duration)/1e6,1) AS ms FROM abnormal_traces p WHERE p.service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND p.attr_span_kind='Client' AND p.span_name='POST' AND p.duration > 0 AND p.attr_http_response_status_code IS NOT NULL GROUP BY ALL ORDER BY 1",
          "claim": "Travel-plan's calls to route-plan minStopStations return 500 in 64 cases, averaging about 7 s."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT 'a' AS p, span_name, count(*) AS n, sum((attr_http_response_status_code>=500)::INT) AS e5, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) AS ms, round(max(duration)/1e6,1) AS mx FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND attr_span_kind='Server' AND span_name LIKE '%travelPlan%' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "Ui-dashboard travelPlan/minStation server spans average about 1.6 s with a 20 s maximum, versus 844 ms normal."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
